1 OCCU Redare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ingela Gathenhielm
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Gathenhielm gifte sig den 2 april 1711 med skeppsredaredottern Ingela Olofsdotter Hammar (11 september 1692 - 29 april 1729) från Hammarkulla gård i Onsala. Ingelas far hette Olof Nilsson Hammar och mor hette Gundla Mårtensdo
2 CONC tter. Det står helt klart att Gathes fru Ingela var en pådrivande kraft som ständigt sporrade honom i hans arbete, och det anses att äran ska även komma henne till del. Efter makens död, gifte Ingela Gathenhielm om sig i början av
2 CONC  år 1722 med överstelöjtnanten Isak Browald (1688-1754), och dog den 29 april 1729 på Browalds gård Lerjeholm.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ingela Olofsdotter Gathenhielm née Hammar
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 11 September 1692 Died: 29 April 1729
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Lars Gathenhielm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingela_Gathenhielm
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingela Gathenhielm was a Swedish privateer in service of King Charles XII of Sweden during the Great Northern War.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1711, Ingela was married to the privateer and pirate Lars Gathenhielm, who in 1710 had received permission from the king to attack and plunder ships from enemy nations on the Baltic Sea (and also, as it was said, often attack
2 CONC ed other ships as well) and sold the valuables of the ship in Dunkerque. He was making a fortune, and was ennobled in 1715. Ingela had met Lars when they were children, as the farms of their parents were next to each other. They h
2 CONC ad five children, and she is believed to have been not only his wife but also his companion in his professional life, and the brain behind a lot of his plans as a privateer and pirate. They both ran the affairs from their base in 
2 CONC Gothenburg. When her husband died in 1718, Ingela took over his Privateering (and his alleged Pirate empire), continued its business and also expanded it during the remaining war. She was called the shipping-queen. The Swedish pri
2 CONC vateering ended after the peace treaty with Denmark in 1720 and Russia in 1721. Ingela married the lieutenant Isak Browald in 1722, and in 1729 was buried with her first husband in Onsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingela köpte tomten på Stigbergstorget år 1718. 
