1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Claes (son of Claudius von Stauden, Adlad von Stauden, Tab. 2), born 1745-07-25 in Karlskrona. Kadett at the Amiralities Damage Tribunal in Karlskrona 1759-05-19. Flanders in the army 1767-08-25. Fänrik at the Russ
2 CONC ian Ladogska regiment 1768-10-10. Dismissed from there 1769-11-13. Located on Upplands regemente 1770-12-08. Fänrik at Hälsinge regemente 1773-03-03. Lieutenant at the very least. 1778-02-04. Dismissed 1784-12-17. Customs inspecto
2 CONC r in Nyköping 1791-04-26. Dismissed 1795-12-14. Death there 1799-07-25. Received permission to travel abroad and visited England, Spain, Portugal, Morocco, Sardinia and North America, returned in 1777. Married 1785-12-01 with Marg
2 CONC areta Christina Hagman , born 1763 1, died 1818-01-15 in Skagerhults Prästgård Örebro County, daughter of the church in Västerljung's pastorate by Strängnäs stifter Jonas Hagman and Anna Margareta Bergmarck.
