1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kyrkoherde i Vesige, Hallands län, Göteborgs stift 1701-1758. Prost 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.klarskov.org/humble/KjaerulfskeStudier.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Ny opdateret: http://www.klarskov.org/humble/KjaerulfskeStudier.pdf Anden kilde: 12. Niels Kjerrulff, born 7. Oct. 1661, at the university in Lund 1684, minister in Wessige 1693, died 22. Jan. 1735. Married first to Ingierd Santes
2 CONC son from Bøkhult in Långaryd, (daughter of regiment quartermaster Sante Pehrsson and Katrina Gyllensten), married second 1711 to Johanna Holtzberg, born 1688, died 1735, daughter of minister Lars H. in Knärød. (her older sister Be
2 CONC nedicta was married to minister Niels Olufsen Kjerrulf in Weinge). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: a. Elsa Katarina Kjerrulff, born 5. March 1698, died 1771, married 1721 to Anders Wetterberg, born 1693, died 2. June 1743, assistant minister in Torup in Gøteborg diocese.
2 CONT
2 CONT b. Marta Susanna Kjerrulff, born 13. Dec. 1700, married to a non-commissioned officer Grønvall.
2 CONT
2 CONT c. Engela Helena Kjerrulff, born 4. Aug. 1713, died 17 . . , married 1736 to Erik Panlin, died 9. Feb. 1755, merchant in Varberg. (their daughter was as mentioned page 66 married to minister Johan Christoffer Kjerrulff). 
2 CONT
2 CONT d. Morten Fredrik Kjerrulff, born 30. Aug. 1717, died 2. May 1785. Volunteer at Skåne cavalry 1737, non-commissioned officer in Adlerfeld’s regiment 1741, Adjutant in Willebrandsk regiment 1743, lieutenant 1749, captain 1750. Made
2 CONC  major 1768 and was promoted at his retirement 1784 to light colonel, knight of S. O. Was 12. Sep. 1772 rose to nobility with the name Kjerrulff von Wolffen. Was owner of Hellerø by Borås. Married 1754 to Marie Elisabet Browald, b
2 CONC orn 7. July 1725, died 17. Nov. 1798, daughter of colonel Isak B. and Ingela Hammar.  Children: 1) Ingela Johanna Kjerrulff von Wolffen, born 19. March 1756, died 1787, married 1786 to Erland Kafle (adl.1
2 CONT  Nr. 70), born 7. Febr. 1753, died 1796, captain in Vestgøta cavalry. 
