2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Ragnar Cederblom
2 CONT * FamilySearch Family Tree
2 CONT * Birth:	Sep 16 1873 - Grava, Värmland, Sweden
2 CONT * Death:	Jan 13 1937 - Mesa, Maricopa, Arizona
2 CONT * Parents:	Gustaf Elis Cederblom, Emma Augusta Wilhelmina Cederblom (born Blix)
2 CONT * Wife:	Selma Cederblom (born Sandberg)
2 CONT * Children:	Ellen Caullvine (born Cederblom), Josta Cederblom, Henry " Harry" Stirling Granville- Cederblom, Gilbert Cederblom, Marie Cederblom, Chester Cederblom
2 CONT * Siblings:	Elis Fritiof Cederblom, Anna Cederblom, Ellen Cederblom
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:G8YL-WCV
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT sida 19, pdf blad 22
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wermlandsbilder.se/Arkiv01/album/karlstads_kommunarkiv/Bio_75_85_KsdHAL_small.pdf 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.se/books/about/The_Tin_Can_Tourist.html?id=21ijEAAAQBAJ&redir_esc=y
2 CONT
2 CONT Citat: Ragnar Cederblom was born in 1873 in Grava, Sweden, and died in 1937 in Arizona. He arrived by boat from Sweden in 1895 when he was 21 years old. He married his wife Selma Sandberg in 1895 and they had 4 children, Marie, El
2 CONC la, Harry, and a younger one who died during the 1918 Spanish Flu epidemic. Ragnar worked as an engineer and draftsman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen Reedstrom is the great-granddaughter of Ragnar Cederblom. She is an artist and musician.
2 CONT
2 CONT Evelyn was the daughter of Ragnar Cederblom and a university professor. She is the translator of the book "The Tin Can Tourist”. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citat: In 1921 Ragnar Cederblom and his son Harry embarked in an adventure across America in a Tin Lizzy. This is the log of their route, the state of the roads, rest areas and towns that they encountered. Ragnar detailed the cost
2 CONC  of everything, gas, food, lodging, and the endless repairs the early Saxon automobile plagued them with because of bad roads and the general newness of this type of transportation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Then in 1925 Ragnar and Harry struggled to build a small house in Arizona, living from meager paycheck to paycheck, being cheated by the locals for farming schemes and trying to find ways to fill their empty bellies while saving u
2 CONC p for the wood to build their tiny house. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This diary contains interesting information as to prices and what an early road trip was like. They encounter coin operated stoves and interesting characters who would offer them the water from their radiator to drink. Ragnar make
2 CONC s interesting comments about the salmon overfishing in the Pacific Northwest and has views on California's emerging irrigated farming. This is a gem for any historian or travel enthusiast!
2 CONT
2 CONT Included is a handy map of their route and a cost comparison chart showing the how much prices have changed from 1921 to 2022. 
2 CONT ---
2 CONT Barn: 
2 CONT Ellen Cederblom 1996-1966
2 CONT Gösta Cederblom 1898-1913
2 CONT Gilbert Cederblom 1900-1900
2 CONT Marie Emma Cederblom 1901-1986
2 CONT Harry Cederblom 1906 
