1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Research notes on her son and partner: According to Swedish household records Emma lived in Storgatan in Østersund while Carl Torsten Blix lived in Prestgatan in Østersund. We know that Emma became pregnant during 
2 CONC her time in Østersund. From the time she became pregnant, no other men apart from Carl Torsten has the the name Torsten in Østersund and fits on age. Carl Torsten was 35 when Emma was 20, and they lived close to each other, in the
2 CONC  same city.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptismal records state her father's occupation as former master smith, and her parents a without a steady place of residence at the time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptised by AW Kvarnstr&ouml;m. At the time of Emma's birth, the family was poor and lacked a permanent address. That same year, the family moved to Stene where Emma's father worked as a laborer.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1880 census, Emma was living with her parents. In October 1888, she left home and moved to &Ouml;stersund. In 1889, at age 20, she returned home and a few weeks later, in July, she had a son. In the 1890 census, at age 22, 
2 CONC she and her son were still living with her widowed father. In 1895, she married the tailor Lars Engman and moved to F&auml;rila. In the 1900 census, she was living with her husband, her son and three more children
