2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/2b/c3/39/5d/5344483f7d893598/dd9eb9436eeae5fe28f1510e28fc2be7_original.jpg?hash=00492df05d1088d18de51375ae79a4a9828d26b3b54c38bd584c979921f2c34e.1795939199
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE Now we are going to leave the Kjærulf family briefly and have a look 
2 CONT at the family tree of the noblewoman Bodil Hansdatter Mørk from 
2 CONT Saltumgaard.
2 CONT There is royal blood in this branch of the Kjærulf family line.
2 CONT It seems improbable, perhaps almost comical, but it is nevertheless a 
2 CONT fact that in the person of Bodil Hansdatter Mørk we have a connection 
2 CONT between the Kjærulf family and the old Norwegian royal line. This is 
2 CONT not as unique as one might expect. In both Norway and Denmark there 
2 CONT are many families that are able to trace their lines back to Olav 
2 CONT Haraldson and Halvdan Svarte. In the Norwegian publication "Tidskrift 
2 CONT for genealogi" for 1924-25 there is an article by C.M. Munthe 
2 CONT entitled "Vore Fælles ahner" (Our Common Ancestors). In it he shows 
2 CONT that a number of Norwegian civil servant families are descended from 
2 CONT Danish noblewoman Johanne Andersdatter til Asdal (Jutland), who lived 
2 CONT from 1385 to 1479. She gave birth to 18 children in two marriages, 
2 CONT and the descendants of these can be found all over Scandinavia. She 
2 CONT herself is descended from St. Olaf, so all of her descendants are 
2 CONT also related to him.
2 CONT As a curiosity we have printed the family tree for Bodil Hansdatter 
2 CONT Mørk. We begin at the top and follow it backwards or down the ladder, 
2 CONT which is the opposite of what we do with the Kjerulf line (tree 
2 CONT included in the Norwegian text).
2 CONT This information on the various lines through the Middle Ages all the 
2 CONT way back to the murky realms of Norway's distant past has been 
2 CONT gathered for the most part from "Adelskalenderen" (Calendar of 
2 CONT Nobility), a yearbook that has collected information about noble 
2 CONT family lines over the years. Norwegian aristocratic families are also 
2 CONT referred to in "Danmarks adels Aarbog" (The Yearbook of Danish 
2 CONT Nobility).
2 CONT Now we shall return to the descendants of Bodil Hansdatter and Morten 
2 CONT Pederson Kjærulf.
2 CONT Bodil Hansdatter became a widow early in her life. As was mentioned 
2 CONT earlier, Morten Pedersen Kjærulf died in 1600, and his widow married 
2 CONT Lars Pedersen, assembly clerk and later tax collector for Kjær 
2 CONT township. Bodil Hansdatter and Morten Pedersen had 4 children: 
2 CONT (listed in Norwegian text).
1 NOTE Vadum Parish Lutheran Church Records.
1 NOTE He continued to live in East Halne, the same parish in which his 
2 CONT parents lived. He was tax collector for the township of Kjær in 1596. 
2 CONT He died about 1660. He was married to Bodil Hansdatter Mørk from 
2 CONT Saltumgaard, the daughter of the tax collector in Hvetbo township, 
2 CONT Hans Mørk, and his wife, Johanne Vognsdatter, from Hæstrupgaard. Her 
2 CONT father belonged to an old, distinguished family of sail manufacturers 
2 CONT (the term indicates a particular process of weighing the sails). Her 
2 CONT mother belonged to an old aristocratic family.
1 NOTE He married Bodil Hansd. Mørk, daughter of Hans Mørk & Johanne Vognsd. 
2 CONT Nestrupgaard.
